#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:4
#: 1baca0eaa74f43bfa45943ed472f68e6
msgid "SBus Servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:9
#: d57ad6abaad346f9a2bf415dbb1ff13e
msgid "`Futaba SBus/SBus2 servos <https://www.futabarc.com/servos/sbus.html>`__ accept the serial `SBus protocol <https://www.futabarc.com/sbus/>`__ and can be controlled by ArduPilot once connected to the autopilot's \"SB\" port or any other serial port.  Up to 16 servos can be daisy chained together meaning that instead of each servo being directly connected to the autopilot, only a single serial connection from the autopilot is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:11
#: 53afa03479ff4eaaba216e2bbc073225
msgid "The transmission rate is 100K baud."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:14
#: bf2a45feec594d279af47d0741f37f50
msgid "Where to Buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:16
#: e1a68f68634d41efaec221d48e4e71a8
msgid "Available from many online retailers including `Amazon.com <https://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_noss?url=srs&field-keywords=s-bus+servo>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:17
#: eb8af4abc69f4fa1a74cb4fd43667e82
msgid "The `Futaba CIU-3 USB Interface <https://www.amazon.com/FUTABA-BB1166-CIU-3-USB-Interface/dp/B01I4KQ0QA/ref=sr_1_19?>`__ is also recommended to allow easy configuration of the servos (`online manual <http://manuals.hobbico.com/fut/ciu-3-manual.pdf>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:20
#: 685af111e8074de48874a3baa714b3f7
msgid "Configuring the Servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:22
#: 4c4b488ba3b34256b35597eb7ebb2499
msgid "Each servo's ID needs to be set to a number from 1 to 16.  The number chosen should correspond to the servo number used to configure and control the servo from within ArduPilot.  For example if the ID is set to \"9\", the :ref:`SERVO9_MIN <SERVO9_MIN>`, :ref:`SERVO9_MAX <SERVO9_MAX>`, :ref:`SERVO9_FUNCTION <SERVO9_FUNCTION>`, etc parameters will be used to configure the servo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:24
#: 09915e3f85364c60a08b1cf5aa9aeaac
msgid "Connect the servo the Futuba CIU-3 USB Interface dongle (`online manual <http://manuals.hobbico.com/fut/ciu-3-manual.pdf>`__) and plug the dongle into a Windows PC.  A prompt should appear to download and install the required drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:25
#: 41d844bd5bc24e1196efda0b40f316cd
msgid "Download and install the S-Link software (`search for \"S-Link\" here <https://www.futabarc.com/software-updates.html>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:26
#: 57e0f2809d9440b3a81184328d525edb
msgid "Use S-Link to set each servo's ID (`online instructions <http://downloads.hobbico.com/software/fut/S_Link_Manual-ENG.pdf>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:32
#: 3b33e96eb1914e2e919464acef4f56a9
msgid "*image courtesy of Futaba.com*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:35
#: bc5dc89064b44c86b622c82b6f206cac
msgid "Connecting Servos to a Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:41
#: 345ae6ad5e5b4c6889c7484f343ab599
msgid "If using an autopilot with a designated \"SBUS out\" pin ,connect the servo to that port on the autopilot.  For Cube autopilots use the \"SBUSo\" port.  For other autopilots without these connectors see the instructions below. The :ref:`BRD_SBUS_OUT<BRD_SBUS_OUT>` parameter must be enabled (=1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:43
#: 9088717ee2964354bf8bd7192280f9cb
msgid "On some autopilots, this pin has a shared function with analog RSSI input by setting :ref:`RSSI_ANA_PIN<RSSI_ANA_PIN>` to this pin. These functions cannot be used simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:45
#: 7abb2623595c480494a3901a478235d0
msgid ":ref:`SERVO_SBUS_RATE <SERVO_SBUS_RATE>` controls the update rate to the servos.  The default is 50 Hz but can be set to any value in the range of 25 Hz to 250 Hz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:48
#: 3c98e89f447745059568437cd3389014
msgid "Connecting Servos to a Serial Port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:50
#: a1a406f109b74f19b555058454a3a15b
msgid "SBus servos can also be controlled from any of the autopilot's serial ports. The protocol uses inverted logic levels (unidirectional: output only) meaning an inverting cable is required when using a standard serial port, if the autopilot is not capable of internally inverting the signals. Autopilots using an F7 or H7 processor can internally invert the serial port's TX pin. Below is a diagram showing a simple NPN transistor inverter which will suffice:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:56
#: e9d0e0397ea946dfa06c80efbc7dfbb2
msgid "Alternatively, a commercial `SPort inverter <https://www.amazon.com/Telemetry-Converter-Pixhawk-Taranis-Receiver/dp/B07KJFWTCB>`__ can be used, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:60
#: 64c6b3c5c0aa4fd9b7620f0e9ff2073b
msgid "do not power the servo from the serial port's 5V, use the systems servo power bus!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:62
#: db26747bd01d4457b349fc83bcbbc8f6
msgid "Set the :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 15 (\"SBUS servo out\") if using Serial2 (normally TELEM2).  For other serial ports use the appropriate ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:63
#: 90e1fdd0a9184916b89d638c5c34abf2
msgid "The port's baud rate parameter (in this case :ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <SERIAL2_BAUD>` ) will automatically be set to 100,000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:64
#: b9a3b7f80c3642c2b0eaf27e829b9a96
msgid "For F7/H7 processors an inverter is unnecessary, set :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS<SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` bit 1  to \"1\" (TX invert) if connecting to Serial port 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:67
#: cb75726a08bb4823bac14d72a51470d5
msgid "SBUS to PWM Decoders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sbus-out.rst:69
#: d8b19a927d61402f86c98cf751d5bd7a
msgid "SBus to PWM decoders allow using the SBus interface with regular PWM servos but beware that some decoders including the `FrSky SBUS & CCPM Decoder <https://alofthobbies.com/frsky-sbus-cppm-decoder-with-pins.html>`__ generate a fixed PWM output rate (~170 Hz) that may damage analog servos (digital servos should be fine)"
msgstr ""
